{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the four sides of a quadrilateral are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c76cc8ea3fec15706976d8736928e2290189fa82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, find the sum of all possible integral values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the 3 smallest sides must be greater than the largest side. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must satisfy the following two inequalities: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/6748b978b4e6eab8203e2a91882003efb7e09694.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3+x&gt;6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/9000aab2f623d5d9b12d13a6a14f66b532c7c5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3+6&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. Solving, we find (respectively) that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3e101763d5fa6ec5ac40b01377a723fcbdda0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/96374814b4d54732d9e39e411a6538167d3dad70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3+4+5+6+7+8+9+10=\\boxed{54}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"324\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">F